@startuml P320_oid4vp_submit_simple

'- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
' Settings
'- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
'=== Header and Footer ===
header OPEN-DID Technical Specification
footer
  	Page %page% of %lastpage% at %date("yyyy-MM-dd hh:mm:ss")
end footer

'=== Title ===
title
	<size:25>OID4VP-based VP Presentation</size>
end title

'=== Options ===
' Auto-numbering: ex) "<b>000." => pads with zeros to display a 3-digit number
autonumber "<b>(#)</b>"
' Hide the participant box at the bottom of the page
'hide footbox

'=== Participants ===
<style>
participant {
  Padding 20
}
</style>
skinparam BoxPadding 20
skinparam MaxMessageSize 500
skinparam MinClassWidth 80

actor "**User**" as user

box Mobile #OldLace
    participant "**Wallet**" as wal <<Wallet>>
    participant "**CApp**" as ca <<App>>
end box
participant "**Verifier**" as vf <<Server>>

box Trust Repository
    participant "**DID Document**" as BC <<Storage>> #WhiteSmoke
end box

== P320-1 : Wallet Invocation ==

vf -> user: Display QR code or deliver deep link (request_uri)
user -> ca: Scan QR code or open deep link
activate ca

== P320-2 : Retrieving and Verifying the Authorization Request ==

ca -> vf ++: GET request_uri
return Request Object (signed JWT)
ca <-> BC: Retrieve / respond Verifier DID Document
ca -> ca: Verify Request Object signature

== P320-3 : Credential Matching ==

ca -> wal ++: Request Credential matching (dcql_query)
return Matching result

== P320-4 : User Consent and Authentication ==

ca -> user: Display Credentials and Claims to present
user -> ca: Consent and user authentication (PIN or biometric)

== P320-5 : VP Token Generation ==

ca -> wal ++: Request VP Token generation
wal -> wal: Generate presentation data for each format\n(SD-JWT VC / mdoc / OpenDID VC)
opt direct_post.jwt
    wal -> wal: JWE encryption
end
return Response body

== P320-6 : Response Delivery ==

ca -> vf ++: POST response_uri (vp_token or response)
return HTTP 2xx
ca -> user: Display presentation result
deactivate ca

@enduml
